    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` (which also runs OpenAPI codegen + MapStruct compilation across all sources) is **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change returns `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 number formatted for humans \u2014 while leaving raw `telephone` in E.164 form.\n\nThree small, cohesive edits following the codebase's established pattern (each derived Owner field is a `@Mapping` expression delegating to a tiny util class like `Household`, `CheckDigit`, `CustomerCode`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`util/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a small self-contained class with one static `of(String e164)` method: strips `+`, splits off the country code (`61` \u2192 2 digits, otherwise 1), and regroups the national digits in threes, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line wiring `telephoneDisplay` to `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\n**Structural impact:** all new behaviour lives in the new util (WMC_other \u2248 0, CC 3). The only pre-existing function touched is the abstract `toOwnerDto`, which gains a single annotation line \u2014 CC stays 1 and no method or class was grown.",
